       Use of bbssdd__ssiiggnnaall() should be avoided; use ssiiggaaccttiioonn(2) instead.

       On modern Linux systems, bbssdd__ssiiggnnaall() and ssiiggnnaall(2) are equivalent.
       But on older systems, ssiiggnnaall(2) provided unreliable signal semantics;
       see ssiiggnnaall(2) for details.

